Subject: [REVIEW 06/16] DPU routing, quad-pipe DSC, plane lifecycle and USB4 sleep ownership

Carry multi-mixer/DSC support, DPU-owned USB4 routing and restoration after power loss, and geometry reset on console transitions. MSM KMS lets the USB4 owner save and stop modesetting before the router stops for sleep and restore it after the router is back; the ordinary device prepare/complete callbacks then leave the saved state alone, and other atomic commits are refused meanwhile. The DSC experiment overrides are removed; compression follows sink capabilities and the link budget. Review runtime-PM references, cached registers and native display regressions.

Dependencies: Base prerequisites. Supplies the DPU and KMS side of patch 07; evaluated with the complete host/display stack.

Source attribution: Jun Nie quad-pipe work with original Jun Nie and Dmitry Baryshkov sign-offs in provenance/display/0040-drm-msm-dpu-Enable-quad-pipe-for-DSC-and-dual-DSI-ca.patch; local DSC/routing/lifecycle adaptations in provenance/display/ and provenance/derivation.json.

This is a review grouping of preserved source, not a new authorship claim or
an independently build-validated upstream commit. Original attribution remains
in the referenced provenance files. No new Signed-off-by trailers are added.

